{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792923913,"nonce":"Cwr0MWOms+jm9Ow0WbiVcBIlr2I=","title":"ASH_GC_STATS reports an empty collector for a program that loads native libraries","message":"A program that loads HDLLs runs on the runtime library (libash_std), which has its own collector and statistics; the ash binary links a second copy of ash_std. The end-of-run report was printed by the binary's own copy, which served no allocation, so it read 'collections: 0', 'finalizers: registered 0' and 'bytes allocated: 0.0MB' while the program's real figures (the ones hl.Gc.dumpMemory reports) were nonzero. ashui trusted the finalizer line while hunting an external-bytes charge (git-bug a1b5f09 there) and lost time to it.\n\nFix: the binary's copy prints nothing when it served no allocation, and before exiting the CLI asks the runtime library that ran the program for its report (hlp_gc_print_stats, resolved by name, when it is not this binary's own).\n\nVerified on ashui's NodeCost probe: before 0 collections, 0 finalizers, 0 MB; after 6 collections, finalizers registered 3291 / queued 2232, 15.4 MB allocated + 12.9 MB external. A plain program still prints one report; ASH_GC_STATS unset prints none.","files":null}]}